      "extract": "Quantum groups (which are algebras rather than groups) provide a generalization of the fa- miliar symmetry concepts encoded in Lie groups. Such quantum groups are deformations on Hopf algebras and depend on a deformation parameter q with the value q = 1 returning the undeformed universal enveloping algebra. First formalized by Jimbo [1] and Drinfeld [2] as a class of Hopf al- gebras, quantum groups have found many",
      "extractCut": true
