      "extract": "A division algebra is an algebra over a ﬁeld where division is always possible, with the excep- tion of division by zero. Nature admits only four normed division algebras over the reals, the real numbers R, the complex numbers C, the quaternions Q and the octonions O. Starting from the real numbers and generalizing to the complex numbers, one has to give up the ordered property of the reals. Generalizing in turn to",
