      "extract": "The complex numbers C with basis{1,i} are isomorphic to the Clifford algebraCl(0,1) which has e2 1 =−1. Given the isomorphism above it means we also have an isomorphism withCl+(2,0), the even part of Cl(2,0). Therefore, via the Clifford Braiding Theorem, the complex number algebra C admits a repre- sentation of the braid group B2. In this case the Artin braid group is equivalent to the circular Artin braid group Bc",
